NAME
    echo - write arguments

SYNOPSIS
    echo [-n] [-e|-E] [ARG...]

DESCRIPTION
    Writes arguments separated by one space, followed by one newline.

OPTIONS
    -n  Do not write the trailing newline.
    -e  Interpret the same C-style escapes accepted by printf %b. A \c escape
        stops all output, including the trailing newline.
    -E  Disable escape interpretation; this is the default.

    Compatible options may be combined. -- ends option parsing.
